  "notes": "Measured on the 787-9 shape from two nearly side-on Commons photos at Beijing: the left side 2025-06-02 (fit within 6 px) and the right side 2025-05-30 (within 15 px: its positions were taken relative to the doors, which put the right side's title ends within 0.005 of the left's). Both sides seen. The rest is ACA/standard's colors and marks, re-measured on the 787 (its own drawing is on the 737 MAX): 'AIR CANADA' x 0.132-0.343 (cap height 0.25 on the left, 0.22 on the right: 0.24 drawn), the roundel and star. The belly line is level from the side, about 2.1 m under the centerline, from behind the radome to where it meets the underside at x 0.835. The fin carries the 2025 recipients' names, drawn as plain bars on purpose to keep private people's names out of the dataset: one thin white bar per row of text (17 rows on the left, 18 on the right, where the last row is a short one starting at the trailing edge), each covering its row's measured extent, from the baseline up about 0.4 of the row spacing. The rows were measured off the full-resolution photos. The right side's rows came out about 0.02 further aft than the left's on its looser fit, so they are scaled to end where the left's do (x 0.975). The fin roundel measured at the same place on both faces, so the fin is mirrored. Not drawn: the fleet number '852' at the fin tip and on the nose gear door, the small registration and Canadian flag under the aft title, and the fin's white leading edge (thin; the fin shape's edge). C-FSBV was still in it on 2026-03-13 (Commons).",
  "history": "New 2026-11-23, split from ACA/excellence-awards (described only), which now covers the 2024 (C-FVNB) and 2026 (C-FIVM) versions. Air Canada painted its 2025 recipients' names on fin 852 in April 2025 (shown 2025-04-08 at Toronto, announced 2025-04-29)."
